                        <span>PRESS RELEASE</span>
                    
                    
                        <span>September 9, 2026</span>
                    
                    
                </div>

        <div>
                
                
                
                    <h2>
                        
    
        Apple unveils iPhone&nbsp;Duo
    

                    </h2>
                
            </div>

        <div>
                
                
                    iPhone Duo features a breakthrough foldable design that’s beautiful, versatile, and durable, opening up possibilities that feel entirely new yet remarkably familiar
                
            </div>

        
            
    
    
    
    
    

        

    </div>







    
    
    




    <div data-component-list="ScrollAnimationDefault AutoPlayVideo">
        <div>iPhone Duo features the largest display ever on iPhone, alongside a reimagined iOS experience.</div>
        
            <a aria-label="Download video: Introducing iPhone Duo" data-analytics-title="Download video - Introducing iPhone Duo" download="" href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/videos/2026/autoplay/09/apple-unveils-iphone-duo/apple-iphone-duo-opening/downloads/Apple-iPhone-Duo-opening-iPhone-Duo-260909.zip">
            </a>
        
    </div>




    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div><strong><span>CUPERTINO, CALIFORNIA</span></strong> Apple today introduced&nbsp;<a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-duo/" target="_blank">iPhone Duo</a>, the first foldable iPhone. Opened, it is the thinnest iPhone ever, with a 7.6-inch inner display that provides a large canvas for viewing content, gaming, and multitasking, and a special nano-texture finish that minimizes glare for an unparalleled viewing experience. Closed, the 5.4-inch outer display delivers 90 percent of the screen area of iPhone 18 Pro in a compact, pocketable design.<sup>1</sup> Both displays share the same aspect ratio, so content scales proportionally, ensuring visual continuity. iPhone Duo is built to last with an innovative hardware design and a precision hinge that offers a smooth, satisfying feel with every use. Powered by the new A20 Pro, iPhone Duo features an advanced thermal management system with a custom-designed vapor chamber and a dual-battery architecture, delivering pro performance and impressive all-day battery life. The advanced camera system takes stunning photos and videos, with the folding design unlocking fun new ways to use the camera that aren’t possible on any other iPhone. <a href="https://www.apple.com/os/ios/" target="_blank">iOS 27</a> is reimagined, remaining familiar and intuitive while adapting to the versatile ways users can interact with iPhone Duo. And with <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/06/apple-intelligence-brings-powerful-ai-capabilities-into-everyday-experiences/" target="_blank">Apple Intelligence</a><sup>2</sup> and <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/06/apple-introduces-siri-ai-a-profoundly-more-capable-and-personal-assistant/" target="_blank">Siri AI</a>,<sup>3</sup> iPhone Duo brings powerful AI capabilities together with a user’s personal context.
</div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Four iPhone Duo devices are shown, facing frontward and backward in star white and night sky.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                iPhone Duo is available in two refined colors — star white and night sky — and crafted from grade 5 titanium that’s been polished to a mirror finish.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/09/apple-unveils-iphone-duo/article/Apple-iPhone-Duo-colors-260909.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-iPhone-Duo-colors-260909_big" aria-label="Download media, Four iPhone Duo devices are shown, facing frontward and backward in star white and night sky."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <div>iPhone Duo is available in two refined colors: star white and night sky. Pre-orders begin Friday, October 16, with availability beginning Friday, October 23.
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>“iPhone Duo is the most transformational change to iPhone since the original. With an entirely new design and intuitive experiences, it shows what’s possible when hardware and software are engineered together and redefines what it means to use a foldable phone,” said John Ternus, Apple’s CEO. “With the largest display ever on iPhone that still fits easily in your pocket, combined with the power of A20 Pro, iPhone Duo helps you stay more immersed and productive wherever you go, whether you’re enjoying content, multitasking across apps, or gaming.”
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Two hands hold up iPhone Duo devices — one folded, and one unfolded.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                iPhone Duo features a 7.6-inch inner display that provides a large canvas for viewing content, gaming, and multitasking. Closed, it’s similar in size to a passport with a beautiful 5.4-inch outer display.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/09/apple-unveils-iphone-duo/article/Apple-iPhone-Duo-display-sizes-260909.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-iPhone-Duo-display-sizes-260909_big" aria-label="Download media, Two hands hold up iPhone Duo devices — one folded, and one unfolded."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>Two Displays, One&nbsp;Breakthrough&nbsp;Design</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>iPhone Duo delivers Apple’s largest iPhone display in an entirely new design. Closed, iPhone Duo is comfortable to use one-handed and fits easily in a pocket, with a 5.4-inch outer Super Retina XDR display that provides 90 percent of the screen area of iPhone 18 Pro. Opened, the 7.6-inch inner Super Retina XDR display is 50 percent larger than iPhone 18 Pro Max, offering an immersive canvas for everything users do. A premium nano-texture finish reduces glare and reflections, creating a matte surface that minimizes crease visibility and feels great to touch. Beneath the inner display, a new FaceTime camera stays hidden when not in use to keep the screen uninterrupted. Both displays share the same aspect ratio, designed for how people use their iPhone, so the experience feels continuous whether iPhone Duo is open or closed. The displays also feature ProMotion, Always On, and 3000 nits of peak outdoor brightness. Later this year, iPhone Duo will support Apple Pencil with USB-C, allowing users to take notes, sketch, or mark up documents on either display.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    





    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>Touch ID is integrated into the side button for easy, secure, and consistent authentication whether iPhone Duo is open or closed, and users can unlock iPhone Duo using their Apple Watch. The design also features Camera Control to quickly launch the camera, including the brand-new Siri Camera mode, which lets Siri see what the user sees to answer questions and take action.
</div>
 

    
    
    


    
    <div data-component-list="ScrollAnimationDefault AutoPlayVideo">
        <div>The precision hinge on iPhone Duo is designed to feel effortlessly smooth — it supports the center of the display to hold it flat when opened, and together with an integrated magnet array, delivers a satisfying and secure closure.</div>
        
            <a aria-label="Download video: iPhone Duo Precision Hinge" data-analytics-title="Download video - iPhone Duo Precision Hinge" download="" href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/videos/2026/autoplay/09/apple-unveils-iphone-duo/apple-iphone-duo-hinge/downloads/Apple-iPhone-Duo-hinge-260909.zip">
            </a>
        
    </div>






    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>Designed for Durability</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>iPhone Duo is built to last and feels exceptionally solid with every use. It’s crafted from grade 5 titanium for incredible strength, with an enclosure that has an elegant mirror-polished finish and a 3D-printed hinge cover with a contrasting micro-blasted finish. Ceramic Shield protects the back of iPhone Duo, and Ceramic Shield 2 on the front has 3x better scratch resistance than the previous generation. iPhone Duo is also splash-, water-, and dust-resistant with an IP68 rating.<sup>4</sup> The hinge is engineered from more than 100 components to precisely control opening and closing and support the center of the display, delivering a smooth, satisfying feel. Internally, support ribs reinforce the structure for added stiffness, while antenna splits with ceramic fiber inserts enhance the frame’s rigidity.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    <div data-component-list="ScrollAnimationDefault AutoPlayVideo">
        <div>Ceramic Shield protects the back of iPhone Duo, and Ceramic Shield 2 on the outer display reduces glare and provides 3x better scratch resistance than the previous generation.</div>
        
            <a aria-label="Download video: iPhone Duo Ceramic Shield" data-analytics-title="Download video - iPhone Duo Ceramic Shield" download="" href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/videos/2026/autoplay/09/apple-unveils-iphone-duo/apple-iphone-duo-ceramic-shield/downloads/Apple-iPhone-Duo-Ceramic-Shield-260909.zip">
            </a>
        
    </div>






    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>The inner display is designed to withstand the wear of everyday use. A scratch-resistant coating and a nano-textured cover layer — made from a custom polymer with up to 40 percent higher stiffness than other materials used in the industry — protect the surface. High-strength glass sits above and below the folding display panel, with custom adhesives that allow the layers to glide past one another like the pages of a book, relieving bend stress, and a titanium plate at the bottom further enhances durability.
</div>
 

    
    
    





    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>An Advanced Camera System with New Experiences</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>iPhone Duo delivers an advanced camera system that brings all-new experiences made possible by its breakthrough design. With the new 48MP Fusion Main camera, users can shoot sharp photos at up to 48MP resolution with zero shutter lag, capture in the 24MP default for incredible image quality at a file size perfect for sharing, and get closer to the subject with an integrated optical-quality 2x Telephoto. The 48MP Fusion Main camera also benefits from a new computational image pipeline for sharp details, and excels in low light thanks to a large sensor, fast aperture, and sensor-shift optical image stabilization.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    
        
        
        
